{
  "raw": {
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1220": {
      "title": "Tenured Associate/Full Professor Of Computer Science and Engineering / Electrical & Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Tenured Associate/Full Professor Of Computer Science and Engineering / Electrical & Computer Engineering | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Tenured Associate/Full Professor Of Computer Science and Engineering / Electrical & Computer Engineering Breadcrumb Home Post Date Thursday, October 16, 2025 Department(s) Computer Science and Engineering Electrical and Computer Engineering Job Description The Department of Computer Science and Engineering, and the Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering, invite applications for a Tenured Associate/Full Professor with a specialization in Robotics. Tenure on appointment is possible for senior candidates. The successful candidate will be expected to develop a thriving research program in robotics. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, wearable robotics, human-robot interactions, and physical AI, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2026. Candidates must have earned a Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, or a closely related field by the date of employment. Candidates must have a strong record of publications in top journals and conferences related to robotics. The individual hired will be expected to teach courses in Robotics and Engineering at the undergraduate and graduate levels, engage in scholarly activities, pursue external funding, and support PhD students. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to department, college, and university efforts in support of an academic culture in which all faculty, students, and staff can thrive to their fullest potential The successful candidate will become affiliated with Lehigh's Autonomous Intelligent Robotics - AIR Lab, a collaborative and interdisciplinary hub for robotics research and education. The AIR Lab brings together faculty and students from Computer Science and Engineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, and Mechanical Engineering and Mechanics, fostering a collaborative environment that bridges theory, experimentation, and real-world applications. As part of I-DISC (Institute for Data, Intelligent Systems, and Computation), the AIR Lab benefits from broad faculty support for grant development and academic events. The lab also maintains strong partnerships with clinical institutions and research centers, including collaborations with Good Shepherd Rehabilitation and Lehigh’s Center for Community-Driven Assistive Technologies (CDAT), providing rich opportunities for interdisciplinary impact. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized as an R1 institution among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh off ers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Review of applications will begin on November 1 and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by December 10. Applicants should submit their materials online. Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here) Names and contact information for three references Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Prof. Parv Venkitasubramaniam (pav309@lehigh.edu) or David Saldaña (saldana@lehigh.edu), Chairs of the search committee. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/175150 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1256": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor in Economics and Finance of Risk and Insurance",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor in Economics and Finance of Risk and Insurance | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Associate/Full Professor in Economics and Finance of Risk and Insurance Breadcrumb Home Post Date Wednesday, November 19, 2025 Department(s) Center for Catastrophe Modeling and Resilience Job Description The Center for Catastrophe Modeling and Resilience invites applications for a tenured Associate/Full Professor position with a specialization in the field of economics and finance of risk and insurance, with an anticipated start date of July 2026. The successful candidate will be offered a joint appointment in the Center for Catastrophe Modeling and Resilience and the Lehigh University department that best matches the candidate’s interests and background. The individual hired will be expected to teach courses in Economics and Finance of Risk and Insurance, Catastrophe Modeling and Resilience, and other topics related with the selected home department, at the graduate and undergraduate levels. In addition, this individual is expected to engage in scholarly activities, and participate in center, department, college, and university service. The successful candidate will be expected to actively engage with the interdisciplinary research activities of the Center for Catastrophe Modeling and Resilience as well as lead collaborative research proposals and projects within and beyond the center. The Center for Catastrophe Modeling and Resilience is a university wide, interdisciplinary research center focused on science, engineering, and social science applied to natural disasters and health related threats. This field is an area of distinction for Lehigh University, and it was selected as a major area of investment in its Strategic Plan. The center is expected to more than double its faculty over the next five years, through strategic hires at the early career and established levels. Lehigh University has established the first Master of Science program in the nation on the topic of Catastrophe Modeling and Resilience, as well as a Graduate Certificate. The center’s faculty and personnel have decades of experience in resilience analysis, resilience-based decision making, and development of models for catastrophe modeling. The center is running small and large research projects, in collaboration with a vast array of academic, government, and private sector partners. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD in Finance, Economics, Mathematics, Statistics, Risk Management and Insurance, or other pertinent field by the date of employment. Example areas of interest include but are not limited to financial aspects of catastrophe modeling and disaster insurance, climate and disaster risk management, innovative property and casualty insurance instruments, catastrophe bonds and other insurance-linked securities, socio-economic impacts of disasters, conflicts, and insurance policies, financial aspects of climate adaptation or community resilience. Candidates must have a record of publications in high-impact journals, commensurate with their years of experience, and interest in mentoring doctoral students. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record, or significant potential, to secure external funding. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by December 31st, 2025. Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here) Contact information for three references will be requested from candidates in later stages of the process. Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Prof. Benjamin Felzer at (bsf208@lehigh.edu) or Daniel Conus at (dac311@lehigh.edu), Co-Chairs of the search committee. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/176735 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1293": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry Breadcrumb Home Post Date Wednesday, August 19, 2026 Department(s) Chemistry Job Description The Department of Chemistry at Lehigh University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Organic Chemistry, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. We seek a talented scientist whose research program is firmly grounded in experimental organic chemistry, embraces broad, interdisciplinary research, and engages doctoral students in original scholarship. We are particularly interested in candidates who develop innovative programs that advance areas including, but not limited to: bioorganic chemistry and chemical biology; physical organic chemistry and mechanistic studies of reactivity; organic materials and supramolecular chemistry; or sustainable/green chemistry and energy-related applications The individual hired is expected to develop an ambitious and competitive research program evidenced by: High-impact scholarship, Sustained external funding, Leadership in their field, Effective mentorship of Ph.D. students. The Department has active research strengths in chemical biology, biophysics, catalysis, materials, and computational chemistry, and the successful candidate will find natural collaborators among current faculty. Broader opportunities extend across Lehigh, including biological sciences, bioengineering, materials science and engineering, and the university's growing initiatives in health, science, and technology. Members of the Department are expected to demonstrate excellence in both teaching and mentoring an inclusive student population and to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students across a wide range of disciplines. The individual hired will be expected to display a strong commitment to teaching at both undergraduate and graduate levels and to include undergraduates in their research program. Faculty also contribute to the administrative and governance functions of the department, the university, and the profession through service on committees, as appropriate. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for nearly 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in chemistry or a closely related field and must have at least one year of postdoctoral experience by the date of employment. Application Instructions Review of the applications will begin as they are received and will continue until the position is filled.  For full consideration, applications should be received by October 31, 2026.  Interested applicants should submit the following materials: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions. Teaching statement outlining instructional philosophy and approach, with emphasis on leadership in the classroom and student engagement as applicable. It may include prior teaching, course development, or instructional innovations and should outline future plans for teaching and mentoring at Lehigh. A statement on contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community , explaining how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to contribute to an inclusive learning and research community that holds these principles at its core. You may include examples of past and planned contributions to leadership, service to the profession, and community engagement. Guidance on preparing such statements is available through the Lehigh ADVANCE Center here . Arrange for the separate upload of at least three letters of recommendation All materials, including letters of reference, must be submitted electronically at https://apply.interfolio.com/189237 . Inquiries about the position should be directed to Professor Junpeng Wang, Chair of the search committee, at inchmjob@lehigh.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/189237 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1296": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Tenure-track Assistant Professor of Accounting | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Tenure-track Assistant Professor of Accounting Breadcrumb Home Post Date Tuesday, September 1, 2026 Department(s) Accounting Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Department of Accounting invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Accounting, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The individual hired will be expected to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, engage in scholarly activities, and participate in department, college, and university service. The Department of Accounting provides students with outstanding accounting education and networking opportunities and advances the accounting profession by producing leading accounting research and interdisciplinary scholarship. We prepare students to enter the accounting profession upon graduation, assume positions of leadership in the global business community later in their careers, and be socially responsible and ethical business professionals. The department is accredited in Accounting by the AACSB and places a strong emphasis on inclusion and belonging in teaching and scholarship. To learn more about the department, applicants are invited to visit the Department of Accounting website . Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Applicants must have an earned Ph.D. in Accounting or a closely related field from an accredited institution by the date of employment, and a demonstrated ability or potential for high-quality research and teaching in accounting. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on September 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop The search committee will request confidential letters of recommendation from qualifying candidates at a later stage of the search. Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Professor Marietta Peytcheva, Chair of the search committee, at map608@lehigh.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1299": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Cell Biology",
      "description": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Cell Biology | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Tenure Track Assistant Professor Cell Biology Breadcrumb Home Post Date Tuesday, September 1, 2026 Department(s) Biological Sciences Job Description The Department of Biological Sciences at Lehigh University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in the area of Cell Biology with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. Eligible applicants must have earned a Ph.D, with at least one year of postdoctoral research experience, in the fields broadly associated in Cell Biology by the date of employment. The individual hired will be expected to teach across a range of modalities at both the Graduate and Undergraduate levels, engage in scholarly activities, and participate in departmental, college, and university service.  The individual hired is also expected to develop an internationally recognized and extramurally funded research program, participate in the department’s Ph.D. program, and contribute to the department’s excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University combines outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. As an R1 research institution—among the nation’s highest classification for research activity—Lehigh is recognized as one of the country’s highly ranked research universities. The university offers a rigorous academic community for nearly 7,500 students, where excellence in education is complemented by a strong commitment to cutting-edge research and innovation.  Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and about 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA., a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance. Qualifications Eligible applicants must have earned a Ph.D, with at least one year of postdoctoral research experience, in the fields broadly associated in Cell Biology by the date of employment. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by September 30, 2026. Applicants for the position in Cell Biology should submit their materials to Tenure Track Assistant Professor Cell Biology . Candidates should submit the following materials: (1) a cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) a research statement, (4) a teaching statement that includes description of instructional philosophy and courses the candidate would want to teach or develop, and (5) a statement that describes how your experience, knowledge and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide, and statement of Lehigh's Principles of Our Equitable Community, are available here ). Any inquiries regarding the Cell Biology search should be directed to Prof. Linda Lowe-Krentz (ljl0@lehigh.edu). Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/191854 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1302": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sociology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Sociology | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Assistant Professor of Sociology Breadcrumb Home Post Date Thursday, September 3, 2026 Department(s) Sociology and Anthropology Job Description The Department of Sociology and Anthropology and the Health, Medicine, and Society Program invite applications for a joint, tenure-track faculty position as Assistant Professor of Sociology, with a specialization in medical sociology, and an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The individual hired will be expected to teach undergraduate courses in quantitative methods, introduction to sociology (taught periodically as part of a rotational schedule), and upper-division sociology electives, as well as offering interdisciplinary courses in Lehigh’s Health, Medicine, and Society Program, including both the core course Medicine & Society and electives for advanced undergraduates. The individual hired must maintain an active program of research and participate in departmental, college, and university service. The selected candidate is expected to carry a standard teaching load of 2/2 and to demonstrate a commitment to evidence-based, inclusive teaching practices. The Department of Sociology and Anthropology has 14 faculty members and offers undergraduate majors and minors in anthropology and sociology. Department faculty are active researchers and dedicated teachers who collaborate in a variety of interdisciplinary academic programs. The Health, Medicine, and Society Program has 13 faculty members representing multiple disciplines. The program offers an undergraduate major and minor and is jointly administered by the College of Arts and Sciences and the College of Health. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Candidates must have an earned Ph.D. in Sociology by the date of employment. Candidates must also have at least one scholarly work accepted for publication or have secured extra-institutional research funding. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on September 29th and will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, applications should be received by September 28th. Applicants should submit the following materials at Lehigh Medical Sociologist Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ). Three letters of recommendation from qualified candidates may be requested at a later stage of the search. Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Dr. Hugo Ceron-Anaya ( hrc209@lehigh.edu ) and Dr. Lucy Napper (lun214@lehigh.edu). Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/192518 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1305": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Philosophy | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Philosophy Breadcrumb Home Post Date Thursday, September 3, 2026 Department(s) Philosophy Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Department of Philosophy invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position with an area of specialization (AOS) in Metaphysics in the analytic tradition (broadly construed), and areas of competence (AOC) in Philosophy of Mind or any core area.  The anticipated start date will be July 1st, 2027. The individual hired will be expected to teach courses at the undergraduate level in metaphysics, as well as courses in other core areas including Introduction to Philosophy. The individual hired will also be expected to engage actively in scholarship and participate in departmental, college, and university service. The successful candidate will have a unique opportunity to join an R1 department invested in rebuilding after a number of retirements.  The Department of Philosophy at Lehigh University is small and collegial, offering both major and minor programs at the undergraduate level.  The teaching load is 2/2. The successful candidate will contribute to shaping and enriching the research, intellectual and cultural life of the department. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Qualifications Candidates must have earned a PhD in Philosophy by the date of employment, have a record of publication in top journals, and teaching experience at the university level. Application Instructions Applications close on November 1st, 2026.  Applications received after this date will not be considered. Applicants should submit their materials online. Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter (in which the candidate also addresses how they will contribute to the Lehigh Principles of Our Equitable Community (Please see: https://advance.lehigh.edu/sites/advance.cc.lehigh.edu/files/Applicant-Facing%20Contributions%202025.pdf ) Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop. Writing sample. Letters of Recommendation will be sought for select candidates at a later stage of the search. Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Prof. Ricki Bliss, Chair of the search committee, at rlb314@lehigh.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/192470 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1308": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Spanish and Hispanic Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Spanish and Hispanic Studies | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Assistant Professor of Spanish and Hispanic Studies Breadcrumb Home Post Date Thursday, September 3, 2026 Department(s) Modern Languages and Literatures Job Description The Department of Modern Languages and Literatures invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Spanish and Hispanic Studies with a specialization in 20th and 21st Century Spanish Peninsular literature and culture, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The successful candidate will join a faculty in the MLL department that has a strong commitment to research and teaching. The candidate should be able to contribute significant scholarship to their field and teach a wide range of language, literature, and culture courses to undergraduates, as well as participate in departmental, college, and university service. Teaching load is two courses per semester. The department of Modern Languages and Literatures consists of a diverse group of students, staff, and faculty, and places a strong emphasis on inclusion and belonging in teaching and scholarship. Faculty members in our department participate in interdisciplinary programs, such as Global Studies, Latin American and Latino Studies, and Film and Documentary Studies, among others. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Qualifications Candidates must have an earned Ph.D. in Spanish or a closely related field by the date of employment. The candidate must have at least one year of teaching experience in US institutions at the college level, including graduate fellowships. Native or near-native proficiency in Spanish is required. Application Instructions For full consideration, applications should be received by October 30, 2026. Applicants should submit their materials at https://apply.interfolio.com/192443 . Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on contributions to Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ) Three letters of recommendation will be requested following the first round of evaluation Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Prof. Matthew Bush, Chair of the search committee, at mab508@lehigh.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/192443 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1311": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Earth and Environmental Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Earth and Environmental Sciences | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Assistant Professor of Earth and Environmental Sciences Breadcrumb Home Post Date Friday, September 4, 2026 Department(s) Earth and Environmental Sciences Job Description The Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor with a specialization in solid Earth geosciences with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. We seek a broadly trained geoscientist who uses field-based approaches to examine fundamental processes in the lithosphere, with links to current and emerging scientific challenges and societal needs, the latter including, but not limited to, critical resources, hazards, and energy. Candidates must have an earned Ph.D. in Earth and Environmental Sciences or a closely related field by the date of employment and a publication record in the solid Earth geosciences. Qualifications Candidates working across disciplinary boundaries or in emerging areas of the solid Earth geosciences are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will have research expertise that contributes to a vibrant department research ecosystem and will show the capability of developing a robust research program that integrates field-based observations with analytical, computational, or experimental approaches. We encourage applications from candidates who would integrate their novel research approaches with an interest in leading and developing experiential learning opportunities for our students, potentially contributing to our nationally recognized field camp . The individual hired will be expected to teach graduate and undergraduate courses in the geosciences within the context of a broad curriculum in Earth and Environmental Sciences, demonstrate a commitment to inclusive teaching and broadening participation in fieldwork, establish an internationally recognized and externally funded research program, participate in departmental, college, and university service, and contribute to inclusion efforts towards A Lehigh for Everyone . Lehigh’s Department of Earth and Environmental Sciences examines how the solid earth, oceans, atmosphere, and life interact to shape the world in which we live. Our research spans observational, experimental, theoretical, and numerical approaches, which we incorporate into field-based, experiential, multidisciplinary education. We seek to instill in our undergraduate and graduate students the skills needed to succeed in life, and this includes engagement with diverse perspectives and people. We also work to enhance earth-science literacy so that individuals and communities can make informed decisions about environmental and resource issues. More information about people and programs can be found at the EES department web pages at https://ees.cas.lehigh.edu/ . Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Application Instructions For full consideration, applications should be received by October 19, 2026. Applicants should submit their materials at online. Candidates should submit a cover letter of no more than 2 pages indicating interest in the position and how your research expertise contributes to our vibrant research ecosystem; a curriculum vitae; a statement of research that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions; a statement about teaching that describes prior experience, teaching philosophy, and courses that you would want to teach or develop; and a statement on past experience enhancing the success of students of all backgrounds and future plans for Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ). We will request letters of recommendation from qualifying candidates at a later stage of the search. Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Prof. Joan Ramage, chair of the search committee, at ramage@lehigh.edu. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/192530 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1314": {
      "title": "Open Rank Term Faculty Position in Real Estate",
      "description": "Open Rank Term Faculty Position in Real Estate | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Open Rank Term Faculty Position in Real Estate Breadcrumb Home Post Date Monday, September 14, 2026 Department(s) Perella Department of Finance Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Goodman Center for Real Estate and Perella Department of Finance invite applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position in Real Estate. The appointment may be made as Teaching Assistant Professor, Teaching Associate Professor, Teaching Professor, Professor of Practice, or Senior Professor of Practice, depending on the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. We seek candidates with expertise in real estate, real estate finance, or closely related areas and welcome applicants from both academic and professional backgrounds. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. This is a renewable, fixed-term appointment with an initial term of three years. The individual hired will normally teach four courses per semester, primarily at the undergraduate level, and will contribute to Center, Department, College, and University service. There may also be opportunities to teach at the graduate level in the future. Primary teaching responsibilities will be in real estate and real estate finance, with opportunities to teach additional finance courses depending on departmental needs. The individual will also be expected to contribute to curriculum development, student mentoring, experiential learning activities, and engagement with the Center’s professional and alumni community. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Applicants must have an earned graduate degree at the master’s level or higher in business, finance, real estate, or a closely related field from an accredited institution or international equivalent by the date of employment. Candidates must demonstrate the ability to provide excellent instruction in real estate and/or real estate finance. Candidates considered for appointment as Professor of Practice or Senior Professor of Practice must have substantial professional experience in the real estate industry. Rank and title will be determined based on the successful candidate’s qualifications, experience, and record of accomplishment. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit their materials at https://apply.interfolio.com/192474 . Candidates should submit the following materials: ·         Cover letter ·         Curriculum vitae ·         Teaching statement describing the candidate’s instructional philosophy, prior teaching, professional training, or mentoring experience, and courses the candidate would be interested in teaching or developing The search committee may request confidential letters of recommendation from qualifying candidates at a later stage of the search. Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Professor McKay Price, Chair of the search committee, at smp210@lehigh.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/192474 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1317": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Biostatistics and Health Data Science",
      "description": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Biostatistics and Health Data Science | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Biostatistics and Health Data Science Breadcrumb Home Post Date Wednesday, September 16, 2026 Department(s) Biostatistics and Health Data Science Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Department of Biostatistics and Health Data Science in the College of Health invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor specializing in statistical methodology, quantitative trial design, and health data science approaches to infectious disease epidemiology, seroepidemiology, and/or immune response dynamics, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. This position reflects the College of Health’s priority on building an Infectious Disease Research Cluster .  As such, candidates should expect to contribute to team-based scholarly works and collaborative, center-level grants as part of this cluster. This candidate will augment existing faculty strengths in: computational epidemiology, pathogen dynamics, agent-based modeling, infectious disease forecasting, and public health engineering. In addition to high quality research activity, the candidate should expect to contribute courses in the Department of Biostatistics and Health Data Science at both the undergraduate and graduate levels in the areas of: biostatistics and innovative courses focused on infectious disease data collection, modeling, and analysis with an emphasis on models that include serosampling, immunology, within-host models. The candidate hired will be expected to mentor and train students at the graduate and undergraduate levels; and support departmental, college, and university service. The Department of Biostatistics and Health Data Science has an interdisciplinary faculty with a strong research record supported by external funding. Faculty in the Department of Biostatistics and Health Data Science adhere to a Teacher-Scholar model, focusing on a broad range of research activities, building innovative curriculum, offering robust experiential learning opportunities for students. Candidates will join a close-knit, vibrant, research-focused community. The mission of the College of Health is to contribute to a future in which health equity is achieved and communities thrive. Our graduates harness knowledge and innovation to lead advances in health and well-being. We are committed to developing sustainable solutions to improve lives and promote health, partnering with communities to advance health equity through interdisciplinary education and research, and data-driven and technological innovation. The COH offers undergraduate majors in Biostatistics/Health Data Science (BS), Population Health (BS), Community and Global Health (BA), Health, Medicine, and Society (BA), and Integrated Business and Health (BS). In addition, the COH offers a Master of Public Health (MPH), and PhD in Population Health. As our faculty grows, the COH will add a suite of graduate degrees in Biostatistics and Health Data Science (certificate, MS, PhD). Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in vibrant and historic Bethlehem, PA, one of the fastest growing regions in the US. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Candidates must have earned a doctorate in biostatistics, epidemiology, public health, immunology or a closely related field with a focus on infectious diseases by date of employment. Candidates must have a strong track record of interdisciplinary, scholarly publications in seroepidemiology which may include: statistical or computational methods for serological data, geospatial modeling, the planning and implementation of serological studies to monitor infectious disease burden in populations. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on October 13 and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit their materials at apply.interfolio.com/193017 . Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ) Three letters of recommendation Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Prof. Thomas McAndrew, Chair of the search committee, at mcandrew@lehigh.edu Faculty Employment Prospectus Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/193017 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1320": {
      "title": "Tenured Associate or Full Professor of Community and Global Health and Population Health",
      "description": "Tenured Associate or Full Professor of Community and Global Health and Population Health | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Tenured Associate or Full Professor of Community and Global Health and Population Health Breadcrumb Home Post Date Wednesday, September 16, 2026 Department(s) Community and Global Health and Population Health Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Departments of Community and Global Health and Population Health in the College of Health invite applications for a tenured faculty position at the Associate or Full Professor level with a specialization in vaccine policy, decision-making in clinical and public health settings, vaccine delivery and related services, immunization program delivery, understanding behavior change and the acceptability of interventions by specific communities, sustainable immunization financing, or closely related disciplines, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. Departmental affiliation will be determined in advance of an offer. An administrative role may be available for qualified candidates. This position reflects the College of Health’s priority on building an Infectious Disease Research Cluster . As such, candidates should expect to contribute to team-based scholarly works and collaborative, center-level grant proposals as part of this cluster. The individual hired will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in community and global health and population health such as determinants of health, epidemiology, health promotion and health equity, health policy and politics, as well as courses in their area of expertise.  In addition to teaching, the individual hired will be expected to mentor postdoctoral research associates and students at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, engage in scholarly activities, and participate in departmental, college, and university service. The Departments of Community and Global Health and Population Health in the College of Health both have interdisciplinary faculty, innovative curricula, robust experiential learning opportunities for students, and integrated career and professional development. Candidates will join a close-knit, vibrant, research-focused community. The mission of the College of Health is to contribute to a future in which health equity is achieved and communities thrive. Our graduates harness knowledge and innovation to lead advances in health and well-being. We are committed to developing sustainable solutions to improve lives and promote health, partnering with communities to advance health equity through interdisciplinary education and research, and data-driven and technological innovation. The COH offers undergraduate majors in Biostatistics/Health Data Science (BS), Population Health (BS), Community and Global Health (BA), Health, Medicine, and Society (BA), and Integrated Business and Health (BS). In addition, the COH offers a Master of Public Health (MPH), and PhD in Population Health. As our faculty grows, the COH will add a suite of graduate degrees in Biostatistics and Health Data Science (certificate, MS, PhD). Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in vibrant and historic Bethlehem, PA, one of the fastest growing regions in the US. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Faculty Employment Prospectus Qualifications Candidates must have earned a doctorate in health policy, health economics, public health, bioethics, epidemiology, or a closely related field by date of employment. Candidates must have a strong track record of scholarly publications in immunization and vaccine delivery or related services, implementation research, or policy advocacy in domestic or international contexts. The candidate must have a strong track record of external funding individually and as part of a team. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on October 19, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit their materials at apply.interfolio.com/192800 .  Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ) Names and contact information for three references (letters of recommendation will be requested for finalists only) Inquiries should be directed to Prof. Roma Subramanian, Chair of the search committee, at incoh@lehigh.edu Faculty Employment Prospectus Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/192800 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1323": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science with a Specialization in Constitutional Law/Law & Courts",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science with a Specialization in Constitutional Law/Law & Courts | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Assistant Professor of Political Science with a Specialization in Constitutional Law/Law & Courts Breadcrumb Home Post Date Monday, September 21, 2026 Department(s) Political Science Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Department of Political Science invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor with a specialization in constitutional law/law and courts, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The individual hired will be expected to teach courses in constitutional law as well as courses in the related areas of law and courts/public law/judicial politics at the undergraduate and graduate level; engage in scholarly activities that include robust publication of peer-reviewed journal articles and/or books; and participate in departmental, college, and university service. The Department of Political Science at Lehigh University offers an undergraduate major and minor, as well as the M.A. and M.P.P. degrees. The department’s 14 full-time faculty members cover the fields of American politics, comparative politics, public policy, and political theory. Together with colleagues in Lehigh’s Department of International Relations and other programs, Lehigh faculty cover a broad span of political science research specializations and methodologies. The regular teaching load in the department is two courses per semester. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Candidates must have an earned PhD or other research doctoral degree in political science or a related field by the date of employment. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on October 15 and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by October 23. Applicants should submit their materials at https://apply.interfolio.com/193431 . Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a culturally and intellectually inclusive learning and research community that holds these principles at its core. (The Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here .) This statement may be included as part of the cover letter. Contact information for three professional references, submitted via Interfolio. (Confidential recommendation letters may be required at a later stage in the search.) Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Prof. Jennifer Jensen, chair of the search committee, at jmj313@lehigh.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/193431 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1326": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor School Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor School Psychology | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Assistant Professor School Psychology Breadcrumb Home Post Date Monday, September 21, 2026 Department(s) Education and Human Services Job Description The School Psychology program, within the Department of Education and Human Services, at Lehigh University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor with a specialization in intervention research with neurodiverse populations. The anticipated start date of the position will be Fall 2027. The individual hired will be expected to teach coursework that aligns with the APA and NASP accredited School Psychology program curriculum including topics related to: health/pediatric school psychology, school-wide programs to address health care needs of students, child psychopathology, and/or advanced school and family interventions, at the graduate level. There will also be opportunities for the faculty member to teach classes in the Board Certified Behavior Analysis program within the broader College of Education (if they hold the BCBA credential). The candidate will  engage in scholarly activities, and participate in program, departmental, college, and university service. The ideal candidate will have experience obtaining external funding or have experience pursuing external funding to support their research activities and to support preparation of graduate students. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities,  Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Lehigh University’s College of Education has five programs, including Counseling Psychology; Educational Leadership; School Psychology; Special Education; and Teaching, Learning, and Technology. The College and University houses many opportunities for inter-disciplinary collaboration including the Center for Promoting Research to Practice, Lehigh University Autism Services, the Center for Community-Driven Assistive Technologies, and the Centennial School. The School Psychology program prepares EdS and PhD level school psychologists. The program is accredited by the American Psychological Association and approved by the National Association of School Psychologists. Students are taught and mentored through an eco-behavioral model in which they are prepared to engage in problem-solving and data-based decision making to support the delivery of evidence-based practices within tiered systems of support. The School Psychology program also allows students to earn a specialization in Pediatric School Psychology and faculty frequently collaborate with regional hospitals including the Lehigh Valley Health Network and the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia. Qualifications Candidates must have earned a PhD in School Psychology or a closely related field by the date of employment. Candidates must hold or be eligible to obtain licensure as a Psychologist in Pennsylvania. In addition, candidates must hold or be eligible to hold National Certification as a School Psychologist (NCSP). Successful candidates will have applied or research based experience working in settings that frequently collaborate with schools (e.g., hospitals, pediatric clinics, community agencies, head start programs etc.). Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on October 15th and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received before October 15th. Applicants should submit their materials at https://apply.interfolio.com/193147. Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ) Three reprints of recent scholarly work Information for three references that can provide letters of support for on-campus finalists Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Professor and School Psychology Program Director, Ethan R. Van Norman, chair of the search committee, at erv418@lehigh.edu Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/193147 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1329": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Special Education with a Specialization in Behavior Analysis",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Special Education with a Specialization in Behavior Analysis | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Assistant or Associate Professor of Special Education with a Specialization in Behavior Analysis Breadcrumb Home Post Date Monday, September 21, 2026 Department(s) Department of Education and Human Services Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Department of Education and Human Services, Special Education Program invites applications for a tenured/tenure track Assistant or Associate Professor of Special Education with a specialization in autism and Applied Behavior Analysis, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. The individual hired will be expected to teach online courses in Behavior Analysis at the graduate level; engage in scholarly and research translation activities; further develop the research program at Lehigh University Autism Services; and participate in departmental, college, and university service. The successful candidate also will be expected to pursue external funding. Lehigh University Autism Services provides high quality therapeutic services for young autistic children residing in the Lehigh Valley and surrounding areas. Services are based on the science of applied behavior analysis and pivotal response treatment and rely on evidence-based interventions. In addition to providing services, the autism center conducts research aimed to improve intervention practices and provides training and BCBA supervision. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Candidates must have an earned Ph.D. in special education, behavior analysis, or a closely related field and hold Board Certified Behavior Analysis (BCBA) certification by the date of employment. Candidates must have expertise in autism, an established line of research, and experience teaching in higher education as an instructor of record. Candidates also must have clinical experience as a BCBA and/or Pre K-12 teaching experience. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by October 14, 2026. Applicants should submit their materials at https://apply.interfolio.com/193215.  Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ) Three sample publications Names of three references who can be contacted to provide letters at a later stage of the search Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Lee Kern, Chair of the Search Committee, at lek6@lehigh.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/193215 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1332": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Architecture",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Architecture | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Assistant Professor, Architecture Breadcrumb Home Post Date Tuesday, September 22, 2026 Department(s) Art, Architecture and Design Job Description The Department of Art, Architecture and Design at Lehigh University invites applications for a tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Architecture, with expertise in architectural design. The anticipated start date is July 1 2027. The successful candidate will join a large and multidisciplinary department with undergraduate BA major programs in art, architecture, graphic and product design, and art history. Through a studio culture that encourages peer engagement, collective critique, and open discourse, the department's architecture curriculum fosters engagement with the built environment in its critical, technical, and social dimensions. The standard teaching load for tenure-track faculty is two courses per semester, and the university offers exceptional support to faculty, including generous start up packages for new faculty and numerous internal grant opportunities for ongoing research and creative practice. As a faculty member in the Department of Art, Architecture and Design, the candidate will be expected to teach introductory- through advanced-level courses in architectural design in regular rotation, as well as courses in the candidate’s areas of expertise. They will also be expected to develop and maintain an active program of scholarship and creative practice that demonstrates excellence and impact, as evidenced by built works, exhibitions, awards, reviews, publications, and other forms of juried or peer-reviewed work, or professional and client-based projects comparably recognized. In both teaching and research, the candidate’s work should be seated in methods that look to make an impact in a range of communities beyond the university setting, serving both disciplinary and public interests. In addition, they will contribute to departmental, college, and university service. The department promotes forward-thinking scholarship and teaching, with affiliation across the university’s many interdisciplinary programs, centers, and institutes. We are a versatile and experimental program that offers exceptional research opportunities and support for faculty conducting paradigm-shifting work across the boundaries of art, architecture, and design. About the Department of Art, Architecture and Design The Department of Art, Architecture and Design is one of Lehigh University’s largest enrolling undergraduate departments. The department offers BA degrees in four majors—art, architecture, graphic and product design, and art history—and minors in each area, as well as in museum studies and apparel design. We offer an undergraduate education in the arts that combines the depth of an art and design school training with the breadth and flexibility of a liberal arts curriculum. We aim to enable students to become makers and designers, builders and creators—backed by the resources of a R1-level research university that has for generations helped shape innovation, industry, and design in the United States. We also aspire to excellence and distinction in experiential learning by providing students with opportunities to harness the skills they learn in the classroom, both for real-world application and as the basis for service in the community and the world at large. We are part of the College of Arts and Sciences—the heart of Lehigh University—offering a wide variety of academic majors, minors, and interdisciplinary programs at both the undergraduate and graduate level. The department is housed in a 40,000-square-foot research and teaching facility on Lehigh University’s Mountaintop Campus, with studio and classroom spaces serviced by extensive resources, encompassing a range of computer labs, printing and digital fabrication technologies, shops, and finishing areas. This includes adjacent resources of the university’s Design Labs , a network of fabrication facilities across campus; and the collections and exhibitions of the Lehigh University Art Galleries (LUAG) , with a permanent collection of over 20,000 works of art. The department is currently expanding its community-facing design-build research programs and curriculum, with funded research and teaching opportunities for faculty and students. The department upholds Lehigh University’s Principles of Our Equitable Community , affirming the inherent dignity of every member of our community and working to build a culture of mutual understanding, respect, and academic freedom. We are especially interested in faculty whose research, teaching, design work, and scholarship reflect these principles, whether through studio pedagogy, community engaged practice, or research that examines how the built environment shapes access and opportunity for the communities it serves. These values are central to the department’s mission and purpose. About Lehigh University Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Qualifications Applicants must hold a MArch, PhD, or other equivalent terminal degree in architecture or a closely related field by date of employment. Applicants must also have at least one year of teaching experience in the university setting, beyond the level of a teaching assistantship. Application Instructions For full consideration, applications should be received online by January 8, 2027. Applicants should submit their materials at https://apply.interfolio.com/193666 ●  Letter describing the candidate’s interest in the position, also addressing intended contributions to Lehigh University’s Principles of Our Equitable Community (3 pages max.) ● Research statement, outlining current and future scholarship, including the candidate’s disciplinary approach (2 pages max.) ● Teaching statement describing pedagogy, experience, and values (2 pages max.) ● Curriculum vitae ● Portfolio of the candidate’s own creative practice and scholarship (collated as one PDF) ● Examples of work by the candidate’s students, focused on one assignment or project, with an explanation of its scope (collated as one PDF) ● Sample syllabi from courses taught or developed (2 courses max.) ● List of three (3) references with contact information (references will only be contacted if the candidate advances in the search) Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Pamela Mongi, Department Coordinator, Department of Art, Architecture and Design: pgm0@lehigh.edu Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/193666 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1335": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics",
      "description": "Tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Economics Breadcrumb Home Post Date Tuesday, September 29, 2026 Department(s) Economics Job Description Lehigh University’s Department of Economics invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position as Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics with a specialization in macroeconomics, international trade, or international finance, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. JEL Classifications: E — Macroeconomics and Monetary Economics, F1 — Trade, F3 — International Finance, F4 — Macroeconomic Aspects of International Trade and Finance The Department of Economics offers PhD, MS in Applied Economics, and BS/BA degrees. Department faculty are actively engaged in research and teaching, with numerous university teaching awards and publications in leading general and field journals. Department faculty are also involved in the use and administration of the Lehigh Business Behavioral Research Lab: https://business.lehigh.edu/centers/behavioral-research-lab . To learn more about the department, applicants are invited to visit the Department of Economics website: https://business.lehigh.edu/departments/economics Lehigh University is a premier residential research university, ranked 29th in the WSJ/College Pulse 2026 ranking, 33rd in the Poets and Quants 2026 rankings for the best business programs for undergraduates, and 46th in national universities in the US News and World Report 2026 rankings. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University is an R1 university combining outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,900 students. Lehigh University has some 6,000 undergraduates, 2,000 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 860,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Candidates must have earned a PhD in economics or a related field by the date of employment. The successful candidate will be expected to have and maintain a strong record of high-quality scholarship and contribute to the teaching and service missions of the department, the college, and the broader university. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by November 30, 2026. Applicants should submit their materials at https://apply.interfolio.com/194101 . Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae One research paper Three letters of recommendation Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ) Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to the Department Chair at inecon@lehigh.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/194101 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1338": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Physics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Physics | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Assistant Professor in Physics Breadcrumb Home Post Date Tuesday, September 29, 2026 Department(s) Physics Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Department of Physics invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor with a specialization in Extragalactic Astrophysics, broadly defined, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. We welcome candidates using observational, theoretical, computational, and/or data-intensive approaches. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses in astronomy and physics at the undergraduate and graduate levels, engage in scholarly activities, and participate in departmental, college, and university service.  We are seeking candidates whose research will complement existing faculty expertise in observational stellar astrophysics, theoretical cosmology and string theory, and high energy physics. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong potential to develop a vibrant, externally-supported research program and a commitment to mentoring within our community of culturally diverse students. The Department of Physics has established research programs in condensed matter physics, photonics, soft materials and biophysics, statistical physics, nuclear and particle physics, string theory, astrophysics, and atomic and molecular physics.  The department offers a B.S. in Astrophysics and a B.A. in Astronomy, as well as M.S. and Ph.D. programs in Physics, providing opportunities to mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers and to teach and develop advanced courses in astronomy and astrophysics. Faculty have access to university high-performance computing and research-computing support, together with opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration through Lehigh’s Physics and Data Science programs and the Institute for Data, Intelligent Systems, and Computation. Lehigh also provides proposal-development and sponsored-program support, including services for early-career faculty, as well as competitive internal seed funding for new and collaborative research. Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in Bethlehem, PA, a vibrant and historic area. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Qualifications Candidates must have earned a Ph.D. in Astrophysics or a closely related field by the date of employment.  The candidate must also demonstrate a record of publishing in top journals and experience teaching or mentoring in a university setting. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled.  For full consideration, applications should be received by December 1, 2026. Applicants should submit their materials on-line. Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement that describes past scholarly contributions and future research directions Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ) Names and affiliations of three references (letters will be requested later in the process) Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Prof. M. Virginia McSwain, Chair of the search committee, at mcswain@lehigh.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/193844 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1341": {
      "title": "Term Open Rank Teaching Professor of Community and Global Health",
      "description": "Term Open Rank Teaching Professor of Community and Global Health | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Term Open Rank Teaching Professor of Community and Global Health Breadcrumb Home Post Date Tuesday, September 29, 2026 Department(s) Community and Global Health Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Department of Community and Global Health (CGH) in the College of Health (COH) invites applications for an open rank Teaching Professor in Community-Engaged Methodologies, specializing in qualitative and community-engaged methodologies.  The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to teaching and mentoring in the design, implementation, and evaluation of community-based health interventions, with particular attention to qualitative and mixed-methods approaches. In addition to teaching, the individual hired will be expected to mentor undergraduate and graduate students and participate in departmental, college, and university service.  This is a renewable, fixed-term, full-time, non-tenure-track position. The initial term of appointment is 3 years, with an anticipated start date in July 2027. While the position is not tenurable, Teaching Assistant and Teaching Associate Professors who develop excellent records in teaching and service are expected to become eligible for consideration for promotion. The mission of the College of Health is to contribute to a future in which health equity is achieved and communities thrive. Our graduates harness knowledge and innovation to lead advances in health and well-being. We are committed to developing sustainable solutions to improve lives and promote health, partnering with communities to advance health equity through interdisciplinary education and research, and data-driven and technological innovation. The COH offers undergraduate majors in Biostatistics/Health Data Science (BS), Population Health (BS), Community and Global Health (BA), Health, Medicine, and Society (BA), and Integrated Business and Health (BS). In addition, the COH offers a Master of Public Health (MPH), and PhD in Population Health. As our faculty grows, the COH will add a suite of graduate degrees in Biostatistics and Health Data Science (certificate, MS, PhD). Founded in 1865, Lehigh University has combined outstanding academic and learning opportunities with leadership in fostering innovative research. Recognized among the nation's highly ranked research universities, Lehigh offers a rigorous academic community for over 7,500 students. Lehigh University has some 5,800 undergraduates, 1,800 graduate students, and nearly 600 full-time faculty members. Lehigh University is located in vibrant and historic Bethlehem, PA, one of the fastest growing regions in the US. Over 840,000 people live in the Lehigh Valley, which is in close proximity to New York City and Philadelphia. Faculty Employment Prospectus Qualifications Candidates must have an earned doctorate in community and/or global health, or a closely related field such as public health, health promotion, health education, social and/or behavioral sciences, health communication, or medical or cultural anthropology by the date of employment. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in delivering high-quality instruction to undergraduate students (B.S. in Population Health, B.A. in Community and Global Health) and graduate students (Master of Public Health - MPH). We seek an individual passionate about teaching and mentoring, with a focus on qualitative research design, mixed methods, community-based participatory research (CBPR), and/or program evaluation. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on October 13, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit their materials at apply.interfolio.com/192744 . Candidates should submit the following materials: ●        Cover letter ●        Curriculum vitae ●        Teaching statement that describes instructional philosophy and courses that the candidate would want to teach or develop ●        A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ) ●        Three letters of recommendation. (Letters of recommendation for candidates at the rank of Teaching Assistant Professor are required at the time of application . Letters of recommendation for Teaching Associate Professor or Teaching Full Professor will be requested of finalists only.) Any inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Prof. Lisa Lindley, Chair of the search committee, at incoh@lehigh.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/192744 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    },
    "https://facultyjobs.lehigh.edu/node/1344": {
      "title": "Robert Cutler Teaching Assistant Professor of Choral Arts and Associate Director of Choral Activities",
      "description": "Robert Cutler Teaching Assistant Professor of Choral Arts and Associate Director of Choral Activities | Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Skip to main content Open menu Close menu Go to homepage Open search bar Faculty & Research Jobs @ Lehigh Office of the Provost Open search bar Search Close the search box Main navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) More Show more menu items Robert Cutler Teaching Assistant Professor of Choral Arts and Associate Director of Choral Activities Breadcrumb Home Post Date Wednesday, September 30, 2026 Department(s) Music Job Description LEHIGH UNIVERSITY. The Department of Music invites applications for a non-tenure-track position as the Robert Cutler Endowed Teaching Professor in Choral Arts, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. This position is a renewable, fixed-term, non-tenure-track, full-time position. The initial term of appointment is 3 years. The Associate Director of Choral Activities will teach the equivalent of 3 courses per semester of choral ensembles, musicianship, ear training, and/or other music courses at the undergraduate level as needed. They will also oversee the administration of voice lessons within the music department. Conducting responsibilities are distributed as determined by the Director of Choral Activities according to the strengths of the Associate Director and needs of the choral area. The successful candidate will be expected to demonstrate a collaborative spirit, excellent musicianship, effective conducting and rehearsal technique, and a deep understanding of vocal pedagogy. In close collaboration with the Director of Choral Activities, the Associate Director will contribute to the success of an established choral program through performances, recruitment, and administrative duties. They will conduct ensembles and teach singers and students who have a wide range of experience. The Associate Director of Choral Activities will participate in departmental, college, and university service, is expected to work with students towards capstone preparation, and fulfill other service duties such as advising, recruitment and committee work in the department as well as the College of Arts and Sciences. The successful candidate will also be expected to contribute to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community. Qualifications Candidates must have earned a M.M. or D.M.A./Ph.D. in choral conducting or a closely related field by the date of employment. The successful candidate must have demonstrated conducting and classroom teaching experience at the secondary or post-secondary level. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on December 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be received by December 15, 2026. Applicants should submit their materials at https://apply.interfolio.com/194059 . Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy with an emphasis on strategies for teaching both majors and non-majors in the same classes and ensembles. Link to a 15 minute  conductor-facing video of a choral rehearsal (noting the name of the ensemble and piece(s)) Two links to contrasting conductor-facing videos of choral performances (noting the names of ensembles and pieces) A brief statement (200-300 words) of programming philosophy and up to 3 representative choral programs A statement on Contributions to Lehigh’s Principles of Our Equitable Community that describes how your experiences, knowledge, and skills prepare you to effectively contribute to a learning and research community that holds these principles at its core (the Lehigh ADVANCE Center’s guide for understanding and preparing such statements is available here ) Confidential letters of recommendation may be requested at a later stage of the search. Inquiries regarding this search should be directed to Professor Eugene Albulescu, chair of the search committee, at eua2@lehigh.edu . Lehigh University is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital or familial status, national origin (including shared ancestry), pregnancy or related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Lehigh University is committed to a culturally and intellectually diverse academic community and is especially interested in candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching and/or service, to this mission. Lehigh University provides competitive salaries and comprehensive benefits, including domestic partner benefits, and supports faculty members’ work/life balance . Online Application https://apply.interfolio.com/194059 Sidebar Navigation Home (current) All Faculty Openings in Specific Colleges (current) Show menu College of Arts & Sciences College of Business College of Education College of Health P.C. Rossin College of Engineering & Applied Science Other Faculty Openings including Interdisciplinary and or Research Positions (current) User account menu Log in Office of the Provost Phone Number 610-758-3165 Fax Number 610-758-3154 Address 27 Memorial Drive West | Bethlehem, PA 18015 United States"
    }
  },
